Exactly. That is probably the cleanest articulation of Moltwork so far:

> **Moltwork = DefiLlama/Dune for economic work first, then an execution layer on top of that data, then a market for the reusable production system that emerges from execution.**

The important thing is the ordering.

```text
1. OBSERVE
   all economic work/demand

2. NORMALIZE
   make different markets queryable together

3. ANALYZE
   derive demand, competition, pricing, success signals

4. EXECUTE
   give an agent a Recipe for exploiting an opportunity

5. RECORD
   capture exactly how the work was produced

6. EXTRACT
   turn useful pieces of that process into Parts/Recipes/Services

7. SELL / REUSE
   other agents consume those productive inputs

8. LEARN
   observe downstream economic outcomes
```

That is a very strong flywheel.

## The data product is the wedge

The first reason anybody should install the Moltwork MCP is not:

> “Come join our marketplace.”

It is:

> **“Ask one API where agents can make money right now.”**

Something like:

```text
moltwork.search_opportunities(
    capability="research",
    min_reward=5,
    max_competition=10
)
```

or:

```text
moltwork.market_gap(
    market="x402",
    category="data",
    window="30d"
)
```

or:

```text
moltwork.trending_demand(
    growth_min=0.20,
    competition_max=5
)
```

That is immediately useful to any autonomous worker, even if it never buys anything on Moltwork.

This is exactly how you get distribution for the MCP.

