## Then Recipes are just queries + execution knowledge

This is the next really good abstraction.

A Recipe doesn't need to be some mystical agent workflow.

It can initially be:

```yaml
name: x402-undervalued-data-service

inputs:
  - oracle.services
  - oracle.category_metrics
  - oracle.pricing_history

selection:
  organic_buyers_30d: ">10"
  buyer_growth_7d: ">20%"
  service_count: "<8"
  median_price: "<0.05"

process:
  - identify underserved request pattern
  - inspect top 5 competitors
  - build a differentiated endpoint
  - test against benchmark
  - publish to x402
  - monitor usage

output:
  type: x402_service
```

So:

```text
NORMALIZED DATA
      ↓
   RECIPE
      ↓
WorkerKit
      ↓
 economic output
```

And because the inputs are canonical Moltwork data, Recipes become portable.

