## And it gives you three defensibility layers

**Layer 1 — Data**

Historical economic observations nobody else has accumulated:

```text
jobs
prices
buyer counts
sales
competition
usage
latency
reviews
settlements
category trends
```

**Layer 2 — Execution evidence**

Not just:

> “Research jobs are available.”

But:

> “Workers with this configuration using this Recipe have historically earned X on this task family.”

**Layer 3 — Production graph**

Which Parts/Recipes/Services actually contribute to successful downstream outcomes.

That third layer would be very difficult for a DefiLlama-style pure analytics competitor to reproduce.

